# What Prettier does **not** own.
#
# The story's criterion is about *source files in any workspace*: "Given any
# source file in any workspace, When I run `prettier --check`, Then every file
# matches the Prettier configuration." Everything below is either
# generated, vendored, or not source — and formatting it would either be
# meaningless or actively harmful.
#
# The two rules that matter:
#
#   * A **generated** file is owned by its generator. Reformatting it by hand
#     would make the next regeneration produce a diff, and the mirror check
#     (`node tools/mirror-shared-to-functions.cjs --check`) compares bytes.
#   * A **vendored** file is owned by its source. `supabase/functions/_shared/vendor/`
#     is a byte-for-byte mirror of `packages/shared/src/`, with a banner
#     prepended, so Prettier will always disagree with it.
#
# The workspaces themselves are NOT ignored. That is the point of the check.

# Dependencies and build output.
node_modules/
dist/
.next/
.expo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated artefacts.
supabase/functions/_shared/vendor/
supabase/seed.sql
# Written by Expo on every Metro start or export (and gitignored).
apps/mobile/expo-env.d.ts

# Lockfiles and other machine-written files.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# The specification trees — prose and design documents, not source.
memory-bank/
.specsmd/
.specsmd-src/
docs/
prd.md
ARCHITECTURE.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.log
